## User preferences

- when researching agent capabilities, the user said “不要只研究产品 UI” and required `能力 → 最佳来源 → repo/file → Atlas 已有 → Hermes 已有 → 直接搬什么 → 最薄接线点 → 放在哪个 X 波` -> make product research evidence-first and source/file-specific, not a marketing summary. [Task 1][Task 2]
- for X7, the user required treating a dedicated laptop as “Atlas 自己的电脑”, including always-on runtime, durable goals, monitors/triggers, proactive/autonomy policy, browser/profile, identities, demonstrations-to-workflows, multi-agent collaboration, crash/restart recovery, remote handoff, and cloud-VM-equivalent execution -> preserve this explicit design checklist. [Task 2]
- when asked for preparation work, the user said “本轮不施工 X1–X7” and prohibited `core/**`, `frontend/**`, `backend-adapter/**`, the Hermes fork, and `tasks/CURRENT.md` -> use an isolated research-only worktree and stop before implementation. [Task 1]
- for independent research domains, the user requested “使用当前环境允许的最大并发，不写死数量” -> delegate independent investigation concurrently where the environment permits. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- `D:\\Atlas` had unrelated C6 work, so the safe prep checkout was `D:\\Atlas-x-prep` on `sol/x-prep`, baseline `9e6d6fde949a0f581ba7e0031004b1f6c4fdd2f4`. The current Hermes dependency pin is `unicorn-Y/hermes-agent@e287231d7906bcce5bc373d20fb2e3e1e6427220` in `core/pyproject.toml`; historical `VENDORED.md` rows/comments do not override it. [Task 1]
- X7 should connect to the existing DBOS durable backend, `AtlasScheduler`, Hub, Hermes `GoalManager`/`SessionDB` synchronization, and `full_access`/`ask_writes`/`read_only` permission modes. Do not introduce a second runtime, scheduler, goal/session DB, skill registry, or permission engine. [Task 1][Task 2]
- Windows design boundary: a boot-start noninteractive service handles health/scheduling/recovery, while a per-user interactive worker handles UIA/foreground/browser actions over authenticated local IPC. Worker loss, sleep, lock, offline, and logoff must be durable explicit states; Windows services are noninteractive by default, and `SetThreadExecutionState` cannot override lid closure or user-initiated sleep. [Task 2]
- Product claims remain vendor claims unless tested. Closed-source dots, Muse, Spark, Grok Bot, Cue, Perplexity Computer, and Claude Cowork are capability references, not reusable source-code sources. [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: validation runs while worker output is incomplete -> `expected three worker evidence manifests, found 1`, `expected seven taskbooks, found 2`, broken links, and only X5/X7 taskbooks. Wait for all artifacts, inspect the complete diff, then validate and repair every failure before claiming delivery. [Task 3]
- Generic `LUNA_WORKER.md` says `D:\\Atlas`, but prep correctly belongs in `D:\\Atlas-x-prep` -> explicitly override worker prompts with the isolated checkout and read-only source constraints. [Task 1]
- Do not mix main-checkout evidence with the prep baseline; every research artifact must identify the isolated commit consistently. Worker limits left X1-X4/X6 incomplete, so do not merge partial output into a completion claim. [Task 2][Task 3]


